[
  {
    "urls": "turn:YOUR_TURN_HOST:3478",
    "username": "YOUR_TURN_USERNAME",
    "credential": "YOUR_TURN_PASSWORD"
  }
]
COMMENT: Rename this file to `turn.json` (remove `.example`) and fill in a
TURN server to make WebRTC mirroring work truly ANYWHERE — even when the
phone is on mobile data and the laptop behind a strict NAT (the ~10% of
cases plain STUN can't punch through). Same-WiFi and most home internet
already work with just STUN (no TURN needed).

How to get a TURN server (cheap/free options):
  * Self-host coturn on any small VPS (~$4/mo): fast + private.
  * metered.ca / Twilio / Cloudflare offer free/low TURN tiers.

The laptop reads this, uses it, AND sends it to the phone over the E2E
relay — so you only configure it here, in one place. No code changes.
Restart the AERIS GUI after adding turn.json.
